The function is already nearly minimal; I only hinted the compiler that the invalid-profile/bounds path is the unlikely one, so the hot path stays fall-through and the two loads issue without extra branch reordering.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect((profile == NULL) || (profileIndex >= profile->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```